# 5️⃣ Async / Await

Introduced in ES2017.

Built on top of Promises.

---

## Basic Example

```js
async function fetchData() {
  return "Hello";
}

fetchData().then(console.log);
```

- async function always returns a Promise.

---

## Await

```js
async function run() {
  const data = await Promise.resolve(10);
  console.log(data);
}
```

- await pauses execution inside async function
- Does NOT block main thread

---

## Error Handling

```js
async function run() {
  try {
    await Promise.reject("Error");
  } catch (err) {
    console.log(err);
  }
}
```

---

# 6️⃣ Sequential vs Parallel Execution

## ❌ Sequential (Slower)

```js
await task1();
await task2();
```

---

## ✅ Parallel (Better Performance)

```js
const [r1, r2] = await Promise.all([task1(), task2()]);
```

Interview Tip:
Always mention performance trade-offs.

---

# 7️⃣ Await Inside Loops

## Problem

```js
for (let item of items) {
  await process(item);
}
```

Runs sequentially.

---

## Better Approach

```js
await Promise.all(items.map(process));
```

