# 8️⃣ Generators

## What is a Generator?

A function that can pause and resume execution.

```js
function* generator() {
  yield 1;
  yield 2;
  yield 3;
}
```

---

## How It Works

```js
const gen = generator();

console.log(gen.next()); // { value: 1, done: false }
console.log(gen.next()); // { value: 2, done: false }
```

---

## Passing Values Back

```js
function* gen() {
  const x = yield 10;
  console.log(x);
}

const g = gen();
g.next();
g.next(20);
```

---

# 9️⃣ Generators + Promises (Pre Async/Await Pattern)

Before async/await, libraries like co used generators:

```js
function* fetchFlow() {
  const data = yield fetch("api");
  console.log(data);
}
```

Async/await internally works similarly:
- Pause
- Wait for Promise
- Resume execution

